      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(footprint \\\"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"59\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(C12-Pad1)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"C12 unconnected-_C12-Pad1_ 0 0.1u\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"The part is electrically dead, since one terminal floats and does nothing for the rail it was meant to decouple. Its footprint does not match a capacitor, which could cause a mis-placed or mis-built part.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.35\n    },\n    {\n      \"category\": \"wrong_value\",\n      \"components\": [\"C1\"],\n      \"pins\": [\"C1.1\", \"C1.2\"],\n      \"nets\": [\"Net-(U10-A)\", \"Net-(Q2-D)\"],\n      \"observed\": \"C1 is 4.7uF/25V and sits between the boost switch node Net-(Q2-D) and the charge-pump node Net-(U10-A).\",\n      \"expected\": \"The spec's EPD table lists the charge-pump capacitor C1 as the G1-group 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V value, and the other pump capacitors as 1 \u00b5F/25 V.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(comp (ref \\\"C1\\\") (value \\\"4.7uF/25V\\\")\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"C1 (G1 group only): 1 \u00b5F/6.3 V\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spec\", \"quote\": \"C2 default: 1 \u00b5F/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 \u00b5F/25 V\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"A 4.7 \u00b5F flying capacitor instead of 1 \u00b5F changes the charge-pump timing and ripple. The part's voltage rating also no longer matches the G1 design value, which could alter the generated EPD rail levels.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.3\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"The netlist shows SKW92A Ethernet pins LAN_PORT3_TX\u00b1 tied directly to GND, which is the most likely anomaly. Smaller concerns are an orphaned capacitor C12 with an inductor footprint and a 4.7 \u00b5F value at the EPD charge-pump position that differs 